<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- THE PRESS LADDER, RUNG 1 — ROW AND CARD, scale 0.975 (handoff README §1).

     Attach to: a settings row, a server row, a sheet row, a subscription card,
     a tariff card, a device card, a payment row — anything the user reads as one
     wide slab. The travel is the smallest on the ladder because the target is
     the largest: 2.5% of a 328dp card is 8dp of movement, which is the same
     amount of "push" 12% gives a 40dp glyph.

     THE SECOND CHANNEL comes from the background, not from this file:
     @drawable/bg_row steps the fill DOWN to ?attr/colorPressBg while the finger
     is held (§1 «шаг фона вниз по рампе»). Attach both — the scale without the
     step reads as a card that shrank for no reason.

     THIS REPLACES R5's "rows do not scale", and the reversal is the owner's:
     R5 existed because scaling a row was found to tear the hairlines above and
     below it, and §1 answers that by scaling every row on a card by the same
     factor at the same moment, so the divider travels with them. What is NOT
     answered by that is the row's TEXT — see PressFeedback, which holds a
     hardware layer for the duration (§11 grabl 1).

     Clock: in @integer/motion_press_in 70ms on ease_press_in, out
     @integer/motion_press_out 200ms on ease_press_out, whose 1.25 control point
     gives the ~2% overshoot §1 asks for. Reduced motion collapses it to 0ms
     declaratively, like every other press here. -->
<selector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:state_pressed="true">
        <set>
            <objectAnimator
                android:duration="@integer/motion_press_in"
                android:interpolator="@interpolator/ease_press_in"
                android:propertyName="scaleX"
                android:valueTo="0.975"
                android:valueType="floatType" />
            <objectAnimator
                android:duration="@integer/motion_press_in"
                android:interpolator="@interpolator/ease_press_in"
                android:propertyName="scaleY"
                android:valueTo="0.975"
                android:valueType="floatType" />
        </set>
    </item>
    <item>
        <set>
            <objectAnimator
                android:duration="@integer/motion_press_out"
                android:interpolator="@interpolator/ease_press_out"
                android:propertyName="scaleX"
                android:valueTo="1.0"
                android:valueType="floatType" />
            <objectAnimator
                android:duration="@integer/motion_press_out"
                android:interpolator="@interpolator/ease_press_out"
                android:propertyName="scaleY"
                android:valueTo="1.0"
                android:valueType="floatType" />
        </set>
    </item>
</selector>
